@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;durability] thread-provisioning-durable
Creating a user thread MUST commit its pending objective, mode, machine
specification, create request key and provisioning job atomically before
provisioning runs. Replaying the create request MUST compare the full canonical
request and return the retained thread, including after archival or reopen.
Retries for the same machine admission key MUST reuse the existing Compute
admission and MUST NOT create a second machine binding.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability] thread-initial-objective-once
After an agent root is bound, provisioning MUST enqueue the thread objective
before marking the user thread ready, using a stable request key derived from the
thread identity. Replayed workers for the same bound agent thread MUST return
the existing agent turn and MUST NOT enqueue a second initial objective.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] thread-archive-deletion-fence
Archiving a thread with a machine MUST persist deleting state, Compute deletion
and its archival job atomically. An admitted VM MUST be tracked before readiness
polling so archive can delete it. Provisioning retries MUST NOT bind a machine
to a deleting or archived thread, and the thread MUST become archived only after
retained Compute history reports physical deletion.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;authorization] thread-current-authority
Every user-thread read, prompt, retry and archive operation MUST recheck the
current authenticated creator, thread grant or team authority through Cedar. A
thread identifier, stale LiveView assign or prior membership alone MUST NOT
authorize a mutation.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability;recovery] thread-reopen-machine-generation
Reopening an archived thread MUST clear its retired machine and agent binding,
retain the original create idempotency key, assign a fresh machine admission
key and enqueue its durable provisioning job in the same transaction. A worker
from a previous machine generation MUST NOT bind, ready or fail the current
generation. A provisioning retry MUST NOT resurrect an archived or deleting
thread, and a replacement for a cleaned-up VM MUST wait for physical archival.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability;recovery] thread-job-key-required
Provisioning and archival jobs MUST carry a nonempty machine admission key.
Workers MUST cancel jobs without that key before modifying thread or machine
state, and MUST leave the current generation unchanged when the key differs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;durability] thread-lifecycle-terminal-read
Archive and delete requests MUST recheck current thread manage
authority under the thread lock. Deletion MUST leave the thread and machine
history readable to an authorized owner or team member, and the thread MUST
remain deleting until Compute confirms physical VM archival.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;durability] thread-retained-transcript-read
An authorized creator, current thread reader or current team member MUST be able
to read the retained agent transcript after a thread is archived, while archived
state MUST expose no prompt admission or terminal write path.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability] thread-ready-requires-running
A user thread MUST remain provisioning until its bound VM has a current running
observation and the initial objective has been admitted. An accepted Compute
request alone MUST NOT expose a ready thread or terminal entry point.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;durability] thread-sharing-generation-continuity
Thread grants MUST persist across pending admission, archival and reopen. Viewer
allows read, operator adds prompts, and manager adds retry, lifecycle and sharing.
The creator's ownership MUST NOT be replaced or revoked through sharing. Only the
currently bound machine may inherit these grants through existing Cedar policy.
Independent machine grants remain additive but MUST NOT reveal a thread; current
team membership retains its existing thread read/write or management authority.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;concurrency] thread-sharing-serialized-revocation
Thread sharing MUST serialize on the thread before its bound VM and persist the
grant change, immutable idempotency receipt and user/machine invalidation hints in
the same transaction. Permission reads from a VM MUST NOT lock the thread. A stale
replay MUST NOT regrant access after later revocation.
